---
// /privacy/: what this site counts and stores (DECISIONS D26). Each claim
// names the code that makes it true. Keep it true: when a claim stops
// holding, change the page in the same PR.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/paths';
---
<Base short="Privacy"
      description="What this site counts, what it stores in your browser, and which other sites your browser contacts.">
  <!-- Copy drafted with AI assistance; needs MCO staff review before launch (UM AI disclosure). -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    {/* No cookies: nothing in src/ sets document.cookie; GoatCounter sets
        none (src/scripts/analytics.ts). */}
    <p>This site sets no cookies and asks for no personal information.</p>

    <h2>Page counts</h2>
    {/* src/scripts/analytics.ts: p, t, s, r (host only), q (utm_* only);
        skipped on Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. */}
    <p>
      We count page views with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, as the
      Station Dashboard does. Each count records the page, its title, your screen size, the site
      that linked you here (its name only) and any campaign tags in the link. It records no
      cookie, name or account.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, nothing is counted.
    </p>

    <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
    {/* MCO.initThemeToggle via src/scripts/chrome.ts: localStorage
        'mco-theme', shared with the Mesonet tools (HOUSE-STYLE §4). */}
    <p>
      If you choose a theme, the site saves it in your browser so the next page, and the Mesonet
      tools, open in it. Clearing your browser's site data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Other sites your browser contacts</h2>
    {/* src/kit/csp.ts lists every host a page may reach. */}
    <p>
      Pages load fonts and shared code from jsDelivr, and read station data and photos from the
      Montana Climate Office's servers. The homepage map loads its code from unpkg, its basemap
      from CARTO and its terrain from Amazon Web Services, and the conditions
      card reads the National Weather Service forecast for the station you pick. Each of these
      sees your IP address, as any website you load does.
    </p>

    <h2>Mesonet app</h2>
    <p>
      The Montana Mesonet app has its own <a href={url('mesonet/app/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a>.
      Questions go to <a href="mailto:state.climatologist@umontana.edu">state.climatologist@umontana.edu</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
